### Page 9 of 11

```text
Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
November 4, 2025
Zimmerman and Lisa Losse; Lisa Losse, Jo Zimmerman and Paul Frauendienst,
residents; and Kelly Zimmerman, via Zoom, expressed concerns about the issuance
of the liquor license. They cited: intoxicated people, road access and maintenance,
private easements used for commercial access, safety, lease effective as of May
2026, site plan process has not been completed, access on public lands, increased
traffic, and effect on residents.
Jeffrey Boldt, counsel for the applicant, explained a shuttle service will be provided.
He said the issues raised are planning-related, and the hearing only concerns the
issuance of the liquor license.
Hearing no further PUBLIC COMMENT, Chairman Malm closed the hearing.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Thompson, seconded by
Commissioner Zwonitzer, that this agenda item be approved.
Commissioner Thompson proposed adding a condition that the board must approve
a site plan.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Thompson, seconded by
Commissioner Heath, to amend the motion to condition issuance of the
license pending approval of a site plan by the board. The motion carried
by the following vote:
Malm, Thompson, Heath, Hollingshead,
Zwonitzer
Aye:
The main motion as amended carried by the following vote:
Malm, Thompson, Heath, Hollingshead,
Zwonitzer
Aye:
Land Use:Variances/Board App./Plats
35. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a vacation of tract 1, High Altitude
Subdivision and approval of an administrative plat known as High Altitude
Subdivision, 2nd Filing, Laramie County, WY.
25 - 526
Atlantis Liberty, LLC, Board Approval vacation and
Administrative Plat, High Altitude Subdivision, 2nd filing
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said Steil Surveying Services, LLC, on behalf of Atlantis
Liberty, LLC, and Jaydenn Bazal, submitted a simple division application for High
Altitude Subdivision, 2nd Filing, and for a replat of Tract 1, High Altitude Subdivision.
He said the subject property is located at 306 Artesian Rd, and the purpose of the
application is to divide the 2.47-acre parcel into two tracts for light industrial use. He
said Tract 1 will be 1.67 acres and Tract 2 will be 0.80 acres.
